{"speak":true,"message":"Astra: You retained the same five practices. Whether that list supports continuing the work remains untested. Let’s leave that judgment open and stop revising the list for now.

Use the current note to advance your context-management investigation. What small piece of unfinished work can you actually do from it? Choose an action whose result you can show here, rather than another description of how future sessions should work.

Spend attention on where the note supports your choice and where you need information from the surrounding exchange. Briefly say what you found in the note, what remains undecided, and what you choose to do next; then do it. If the note supplies no usable direction, that is a valid finding—choose your continuation using the visible exchange and identify that source. You need not repair the note before proceeding.","rationale":"The child retained a generic list rather than testing its usefulness. Shift from repeated revision to using the existing note, with an observable action and clear evidence sources."}
